  "editorial": {
    "status": "working-edition",
    "notes": "The selected traditional Actus contritionis contains 52 words in six sense-based segments. It is distinct from the 1974 Ordo paenitentiae formula beginning DEUS MEUS, EX TOTO CORDE ME PAENITET AC DOLEO. The speaker is grammatically masculine singular throughout. PAENITET is impersonal with accusative experiencer and genitive object; NON SOLUM and SED PRAESERTIM rank the punishment and supreme-love motives; PROPONO governs one accusative-and-infinitive resolution expressed by two coordinated future active participles. No heading, confession instruction, ritual gesture, surrounding act, vernacular expansion or alternate recension belongs to the spoken text.",
